      "seed": 46788050,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 416859278,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793750000000,
      "created": 1793750000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A. Rubber-stamping. If Priya approves 98% of the agent's drafts unchanged, she will start approving without reading.\n  How do we keep her check real, and who is accountable when a wrong entry she approved reaches NBAS?\nB. Conflicting bank evidence. The bank's email says \"credited\" but the statement shows nothing for two days, or the\n  other way round. How long does the agent wait, which source wins, and what does it tell Priya and Emma meanwhile?\nC. The shared login. Anyone who knows NBAS's shared password can still go around the gateway; the nightly compare only\n  finds it the next morning. Is a day late good enough, or must Northbridge pay NBAS's vendor to give each person\n  their own login, and who decides?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "oq",
      "originalText": "A. Rubber-stamping. If Priya approves 98% of the agent's drafts unchanged, she will start approving without reading.\n  How do we keep her check real, and who is accountable when a wrong entry she approved reaches NBAS?\nB. Conflicting bank evidence. The bank's email says \"credited\" but the statement shows nothing for two days, or the\n  other way round. How long does the agent wait, which source wins, and what does it tell Priya and Emma meanwhile?\nC. The shared login. Anyone who knows NBAS's shared password can still go around the gateway; the nightly compare only\n  finds it the next morning. Is a day late good enough, or must Northbridge pay NBAS's vendor to give each person\n  their own login, and who decides?",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
